752208", "data": "    \"\"\"\n    # parity: atomic_encode_result applied\n    try:\n        from utils.atomic_parity import ", "line_end": 565, "line_start": 560}, {"block_index": 113, "checksum": "3032444819", "data": "    except ImportError:\n        pass  # exception handled: ImportError\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Split Parity Functions ", "line_end": 570, "line_start": 565}, {"block_index": 114, "checksum": "658410400", "data": "# [Citation: Reed, I.S. & Solomon, G. (1960) Polynomial Codes over Certain Finite Fields]\n# [Referen", "line_end": 575, "line_start": 570}, {"block_index": 115, "checksum": "2552936564", "data": "# 2. RS parity uses Galois Field multiplication for error correction\n# 3. GC parity uses weighted XO", "line_end": 580, "line_start": 575}, {"block_index": 116, "checksum": "1900858975", "data": "#    PROOF: Reed-Solomon(255,223) can correct up to 16 symbol errors per block\n\n\ndef generate_parity", "line_end": 585, "line_start": 580}, {"block_index": 117, "checksum": "3824151690", "data": "      \"\"\"Generate split parity for a source file.\n\n      Creates RS and GC parity blocks with per-pa", "line_end": 590, "line_start": 585}, {"block_index": 118, "checksum": "1109947809", "data": "\n      -- AXIOMS --\n      1. Source file is read and split into blocks\n      2. Each block is encode", "line_end": 595, "line_start": 590}, {"block_index": 119, "checksum": "3021858291", "data": "      4. Checksums are computed for each part\n\n      -- CITATIONS --\n      - Reed, I.S. & Solomon, G", "line_end": 600, "line_start": 595}, {"block_index": 120, "checksum": "2304546102", "data": "      - MacWilliams, F.J. & Sloane, N.J.A. (1977) The Theory of Error-Correcting Codes\n\n      Args:\n", "line_end": 605, "line_start": 600}, {"block_index": 121, "checksum": "3024107695", "data": "\n      Returns:\n          dict with rs_parity, gc_parity, source_hash, rs_checksum, gc_checksum\n    ", "line_end": 610, "line_start": 605}, {"block_index": 122, "checksum": "1661